# ── ListingLabs deploy repo — SECURITY-FIRST WHITELIST ───────────────────────
# The repo root is the `verifysheet` folder, but ONLY the folders the site build
# needs are tracked. Everything else here stays private and is NEVER uploaded.
# This whitelist is the guard: nothing outside the paths re-included below can be
# committed by accident, even if you run `git add .`.

# 1) Ignore EVERYTHING at the repo root first...
/*

# 2) ...then re-include only what the build needs.
#    (No trailing slash on the negations — that form reliably re-includes the
#     directory AND its contents across git versions.)
!/perps_correlation
!/cache
!/.github
!/.gitignore
!/README.md

# 3) Context / developer docs are LOCAL-ONLY. The public repo gets the code the
#    cloud build needs — not the manual for how to operate it.
**/CLAUDE.md
perps_correlation/docs/
perps_correlation/study/HOW_TO_RUN.md
perps_correlation/study/EXPLANATION.txt

# 4) Inside those folders, still drop noise and anything secret-shaped
#    (defense in depth — secrets live outside the repo, but never take chances).
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/
**/*.env
**/secrets*
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*credential*

# 5) Drop heavy / regenerated artifacts the live site doesn't need. Excluding the
#    logs + notebooks also shrinks the surface where a stray key could hide.
perps_correlation/Listinglabs.zip
# The built site is published as a Pages artifact every run (never read from git),
# so tracking it would just churn HTML into history forever.
perps_correlation/Listinglabs/
perps_correlation/*.log
perps_correlation/**/*.log
perps_correlation/*.ipynb
perps_correlation/*.docx
cache/audit_run.log
# Full-depth local signal extraction (tools/extract_signal_data.py) — heavy
# hourly OI/kline series, regenerable on demand; kept local, never committed.
cache/screener/raw/
cache/screener/extract_report.json

# 6) LOCAL-ONLY signal-research / edge tools. The tuned thresholds + pump model
#    ARE the edge — keep them OFF the public repo. These run on the PC (and on the
#    box via scp), never from git, so ignoring them breaks nothing. Defense in
#    depth: they are also never `git add`ed by hand. (extract_signal_data.py stays
#    tracked — it is pure data plumbing with no edge, and the box pulls it.)
perps_correlation/tools/backtest_signals.py
perps_correlation/tools/optimize_signals.py
perps_correlation/tools/grade_fires.py
perps_correlation/tools/signal_loop.py
perps_correlation/tools/pump_score.py
# PC-side private backup/recovery of the hourly training series (local automation)
perps_correlation/tools/backup_hourly_series.py
perps_correlation/tools/backfill_hourly_series.py
